        <!-- Renal Replacement Therapy -->
        <div id="renal-replacement-therapy" class="flip-card h-64 cursor-pointer">
          <div class="flip-card-inner">
            <div class="flip-card-front bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-6 border border-gray-200">
              <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-4 text-gray-800 flex items-center justify-between">
                renal_replacement_therapy
                <span class="text-xs text-gray-500">Click to flip</span>
              </h4>
              <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 space-y-2">
                <li>• RRT mode category mapping (mCIDE)</li>
                <li>• Unit conversions to CLIF standards</li>
                <li>• Verify missingness by modality</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="flip-card-back bg-clif-burgundy rounded-lg shadow-md p-6 text-white overflow-y-auto">
              <button class="modal-close" aria-label="Close">×</button>
              <h4 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Renal Replacement Therapy</h4>

              <div class="expanded-content">
                <div class="space-y-6">
                  <!-- Important Notes -->
                  <div class="bg-yellow-500/20 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-400/30">
                    <h5 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2 text-yellow-300">Important Notes (3.0)</h5>
                    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
                      <li>• The table now covers both continuous RRT (CRRT) modes and intermittent hemodialysis. Two new identifier columns: <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">device_id</code> (unique ID of the individual dialysis machine, e.g. ACZ3RV91) and <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">dialysis_machine_name</code> (the machine's brand or model name)</li>
                      <li>• Two new dialysate-bath columns: <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">potassium_bath</code> (integer, mEq/L, 0–4) and <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">calcium_bath</code> (float, mEq/L, 0–4). These distinguish <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">ihd</code> (dialysate bath contains potassium and calcium, so both fields are populated) from <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">iuf</code> (no dialysate bath, so both fields are null)</li>
                      <li>• This table records machine settings and rates, not fluid volumes. There is no <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">ultrafiltration_out</code> column in 3.0: net ultrafiltration (fluid removed from the patient) goes in the <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">output</code> table under <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">output_group = ultrafiltration</code>, and replacement/dialysate fluids delivered go in the <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">input</code> table under <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">input_group = renal_replacement_fluids</code></li>
                    </ul>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 1 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 1: Create RRT Mode Mappings</h5>
                    <p class="text-sm mb-3">Before transforming your RRT data, prepare the mapping file:</p>
                    <div class="space-y-3 text-sm">
                      <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg">
                        <p><strong class="text-blue-300">Mode Category Mapping:</strong> Map all site-specific <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">mode_name</code> values to standardized CLIF <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">mode_category</code> values. Permissible values: <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">scuf</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">cvvh</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">cvvhd</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">cvvhdf</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">avvh</code> (accelerated veno-venous hemofiltration, also called ARRT or PIRRT), <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">ihd</code> (intermittent hemodialysis), <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">iuf</code> (isolated ultrafiltration)</p>
                        <a href="https://github.com/Common-Longitudinal-ICU-data-Format/CLIF/blob/3.0/mCIDE/renal_replacement_therapy/clif_renal_replacement_therapy_mode_categories.csv" target="_blank" class="text-blue-300 hover:underline text-xs mt-1 inline-block">→ clif_renal_replacement_therapy_mode_categories.csv</a>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 2 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 2: Filter to Inpatient Hospitalizations</h5>
                    <p class="text-sm">Filter your RRT data to include only inpatient hospitalizations.</p>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 3 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 3: Apply Mappings</h5>
                    <p class="text-sm">Join the mapping file created in Step 1 to your RRT table to add the <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">mode_category</code> column.</p>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 4 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 4: Unit Conversions</h5>
                    <div class="bg-yellow-500/20 p-3 rounded-lg border border-yellow-400/30 text-sm mb-3">
                      <p class="text-yellow-300 font-semibold mb-2">Critical Requirement:</p>
                      <p class="text-sm">All RRT parameters must be reported using CLIF units. Please refer to the data dictionary page for RRT setting units.</p>
                    </div>
                    <p class="text-sm mb-3">If your source data uses different units, convert to CLIF standards. Eg:</p>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-sm">
                      <table class="text-xs w-full">
                        <thead>
                          <tr class="border-b border-white/20">
                            <th class="text-left py-1 pr-2">Parameter</th>
                            <th class="text-left py-1 pr-2">CLIF Unit</th>
                            <th class="text-left py-1">Conversion Example</th>
                          </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                          <tr class="border-b border-white/10">
                            <td class="py-1 pr-2"><code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">blood_flow_rate</code></td>
                            <td class="py-1 pr-2 text-green-300">mL/min</td>
                            <td class="py-1 text-gray-300">0.2 L/min → 200 mL/min</td>
                          </tr>
                          <tr class="border-b border-white/10">
                            <td class="py-1 pr-2"><code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">pre_filter_replacement_fluid_rate</code></td>
                            <td class="py-1 pr-2 text-green-300">mL/hr</td>
                            <td class="py-1 text-gray-300">1 L/hr → 1000 mL/hr (CRRT modes only; null for ihd/iuf)</td>
                          </tr>
                          <tr class="border-b border-white/10">
                            <td class="py-1 pr-2"><code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">post_filter_replacement_fluid_rate</code></td>
                            <td class="py-1 pr-2 text-green-300">mL/hr</td>
                            <td class="py-1 text-gray-300">0.5 L/hr → 500 mL/hr (CRRT modes only; null for ihd/iuf)</td>
                          </tr>
                          <tr class="border-b border-white/10">
                            <td class="py-1 pr-2"><code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">dialysate_flow_rate</code></td>
                            <td class="py-1 pr-2 text-green-300">mL/hr</td>
                            <td class="py-1 text-gray-300">2 L/hr → 2000 mL/hr; IHD sources often record mL/min, so multiply by 60 (500 mL/min → 30000 mL/hr)</td>
                          </tr>
                          <tr>
                            <td class="py-1 pr-2"><code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">potassium_bath</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">calcium_bath</code></td>
                            <td class="py-1 pr-2 text-green-300">mEq/L</td>
                            <td class="py-1 text-gray-300">Dialysate bath concentrations, range 0–4</td>
                          </tr>
                        </tbody>
                      </table>
                      <p class="text-xs mt-2 text-gray-300">Ultrafiltration volume is not a column in this table; record it in the <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">output</code> table (<code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">output_group = ultrafiltration</code>).</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="space-y-6">
                  <!-- Step 5 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 5: Verify Missingness by Modality</h5>
                    <p class="text-sm mb-3">Validate that parameter availability matches the expected pattern for each <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">mode_category</code> (from the 3.0 data dictionary):</p>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-2 rounded-lg overflow-x-auto">
                      <table class="text-xs w-full">
                        <thead>
                          <tr class="border-b border-white/20">
                            <th class="px-2 py-1 text-left">mode_category</th>
                            <th class="px-2 py-1 text-left">Blood Flow</th>
                            <th class="px-2 py-1 text-left">Pre-Filter</th>
                            <th class="px-2 py-1 text-left">Post-Filter</th>
                            <th class="px-2 py-1 text-left">Dialysate</th>
                          </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody class="text-xs">
                          <tr class="border-b border-white/10"><td class="px-2 py-1 font-semibold">scuf</td><td class="px-2 py-1 text-green-300">E</td><td class="px-2 py-1"></td><td class="px-2 py-1"></td><td class="px-2 py-1"></td></tr>
                          <tr class="border-b border-white/10"><td class="px-2 py-1 font-semibold">cvvh</td><td class="px-2 py-1 text-green-300">E</td><td class="px-2 py-1 text-green-300">E</td><td class="px-2 py-1 text-green-300">E</td><td class="px-2 py-1"></td></tr>
                          <tr class="border-b border-white/10"><td class="px-2 py-1 font-semibold">cvvhd</td><td class="px-2 py-1 text-green-300">E</td><td class="px-2 py-1"></td><td class="px-2 py-1"></td><td class="px-2 py-1 text-green-300">E</td></tr>
                          <tr class="border-b border-white/10"><td class="px-2 py-1 font-semibold">cvvhdf</td><td class="px-2 py-1 text-green-300">E</td><td class="px-2 py-1 text-green-300">E</td><td class="px-2 py-1 text-green-300">E</td><td class="px-2 py-1 text-green-300">E</td></tr>
                          <tr class="border-b border-white/10"><td class="px-2 py-1 font-semibold">avvh <span class="font-normal text-gray-300">(VVH variant)</span></td><td class="px-2 py-1 text-green-300">E</td><td class="px-2 py-1 text-yellow-300">P</td><td class="px-2 py-1 text-yellow-300">P</td><td class="px-2 py-1"></td></tr>
                          <tr class="border-b border-white/10"><td class="px-2 py-1 font-semibold">avvh <span class="font-normal text-gray-300">(VVHD variant)</span></td><td class="px-2 py-1 text-green-300">E</td><td class="px-2 py-1"></td><td class="px-2 py-1"></td><td class="px-2 py-1 text-yellow-300">P</td></tr>
                          <tr class="border-b border-white/10"><td class="px-2 py-1 font-semibold">avvh <span class="font-normal text-gray-300">(VVHF variant)</span></td><td class="px-2 py-1 text-green-300">E</td><td class="px-2 py-1 text-yellow-300">P</td><td class="px-2 py-1 text-yellow-300">P</td><td class="px-2 py-1 text-yellow-300">P</td></tr>
                          <tr class="border-b border-white/10"><td class="px-2 py-1 font-semibold">ihd</td><td class="px-2 py-1 text-green-300">E</td><td class="px-2 py-1"></td><td class="px-2 py-1"></td><td class="px-2 py-1 text-green-300">E</td></tr>
                          <tr><td class="px-2 py-1 font-semibold">iuf</td><td class="px-2 py-1 text-green-300">E</td><td class="px-2 py-1"></td><td class="px-2 py-1"></td><td class="px-2 py-1 text-green-300">E</td></tr>
                        </tbody>
                      </table>
                      <p class="text-xs mt-2 text-gray-300"><span class="text-green-300">E</span> = Required | <span class="text-yellow-300">P</span> = May be used | Empty = Not used (leave null)</p>
                      <p class="text-xs mt-2 text-gray-300">All three AVVH variants map to <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">mode_category = avvh</code>. <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">ihd</code> and <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">iuf</code> share the same rate columns; tell them apart by <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">potassium_bath</code> / <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">calcium_bath</code> (populated for ihd, null for iuf).</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 6 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 6: Final Cleanup</h5>
                    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">•</span>
                        <strong>Deduplicate:</strong> Remove duplicate rows
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">•</span>
                        <strong>UTC Conversion:</strong> Convert all datetime fields to UTC timezone
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">•</span>
                        <strong>Data Types:</strong> Ensure all variables match data dictionary specifications
                      </li>
                    </ul>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Data Quality Checks -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Data Quality Checks</h5>
                    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">✓</span>
                        Validate <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">mode_category</code> mappings against mCIDE
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">✓</span>
                        Verify parameter missingness aligns with modality expectations
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">✓</span>
                        Check unit conversions are applied correctly
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">✓</span>
                        Confirm <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">potassium_bath</code> and <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">calcium_bath</code> are populated for <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">ihd</code> rows and null for <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">iuf</code> rows
                      </li>
                    </ul>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Hospital Diagnosis -->
        <div id="hospital-diagnosis" class="flip-card h-64 cursor-pointer">
          <div class="flip-card-inner">
            <div class="flip-card-front bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-6 border border-gray-200">
              <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-4 text-gray-800 flex items-center justify-between">
                hospital_diagnosis
                <span class="text-xs text-gray-500">Click to flip</span>
              </h4>
              <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 space-y-2">
                <li>• Primary vs secondary diagnosis assignment</li>
                <li>• Present on admission (POA) filtering</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="flip-card-back bg-clif-burgundy rounded-lg shadow-md p-6 text-white overflow-y-auto">
              <button class="modal-close" aria-label="Close">×</button>
              <h4 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Hospital Diagnosis</h4>

              <div class="expanded-content">
                <div class="space-y-6">
                  <!-- Important Notes -->
                  <div class="bg-yellow-500/20 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-400/30">
                    <h5 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2 text-yellow-300">Important Notes</h5>
                    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
                      <li>• This table only includes <strong>finalized billing diagnosis codes</strong> for hospital reimbursement (e.g., for Diagnosis Related Group calculation)</li>
                      <li>• These diagnoses have <strong>no timestamps</strong> because they are usually finalized after discharge. Use them for comorbidity scores, not as input features for predicting an inpatient event</li>
                      <li>• All other diagnosis codes for a patient are included in the alpha table <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">patient_diagnosis</code>, which has start and end timestamps</li>
                    </ul>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 1 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 1: Filter to Inpatient Hospitalizations</h5>
                    <p class="text-sm">Filter your hospital diagnosis data to include only inpatient hospitalizations. Every <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">hospitalization_id</code> must match one in your CLIF <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">hospitalization</code> table.</p>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 2 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 2: Create Primary Diagnosis Flag</h5>
                    <p class="text-sm mb-3">If your source data has diagnosis ranking, create the <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">diagnosis_primary</code> column:</p>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-sm">
                      <ul class="space-y-2">
                        <li><strong class="text-green-300">1</strong> = Primary diagnosis (rank = 1)</li>
                        <li><strong class="text-yellow-300">0</strong> = Secondary diagnosis (rank ≥ 2)</li>
                      </ul>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="space-y-6">
                  <!-- Step 3 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 3: Filter and Assign POA Values</h5>
                    <p class="text-sm mb-3">Only include rows where <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">poa_present</code> is definitively Yes or No:</p>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-sm mb-3">
                      <p class="text-red-300 font-semibold mb-2">Exclude rows with:</p>
                      <p class="text-xs">Unknown, Null, Missing, Clinically Undetermined, Exempt from POA Reporting, Unspecified, etc.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-sm">
                      <p class="text-green-300 font-semibold mb-2">Assign values:</p>
                      <ul class="space-y-1">
                        <li><strong class="text-green-300">1</strong> = Yes (present on admission)</li>
                        <li><strong class="text-yellow-300">0</strong> = No (not present on admission)</li>
                      </ul>
                      <p class="text-xs mt-2 text-gray-300">No other values are permitted.</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 4 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 4: Final Cleanup</h5>
                    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">•</span>
                        <strong>Deduplicate:</strong> Remove duplicate rows
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">•</span>
                        <span><strong>Code Format:</strong> Populate <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">diagnosis_code_format</code> for every row alongside <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">diagnosis_code</code>. Only two values are allowed: <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">ICD10CM</code> or <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">ICD9CM</code>. This table has no datetime columns, so no UTC conversion is needed</span>
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">•</span>
                        <strong>Data Types:</strong> Ensure all variables match data dictionary specifications
                      </li>
                    </ul>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Data Quality Checks -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Data Quality Checks</h5>
                    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">✓</span>
                        Verify <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">diagnosis_primary</code> contains only 0 or 1
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">✓</span>
                        Verify <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">poa_present</code> contains only 0 or 1
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">✓</span>
                        Validate <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">diagnosis_code</code> is a valid ICD-9-CM or ICD-10-CM code and that <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">diagnosis_code_format</code> (ICD9CM / ICD10CM) matches it
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">✓</span>
                        Ensure all <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">hospitalization_id</code> values exist in the <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">hospitalization</code> table
                      </li>
                    </ul>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Hospitalization -->
        <div id="hospitalization" class="flip-card h-64 cursor-pointer">
          <div class="flip-card-inner">
            <div class="flip-card-front bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-6 border border-gray-200">
              <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-4 text-gray-800 flex items-center justify-between">
                hospitalization
                <span class="text-xs text-gray-500">Click to flip</span>
              </h4>
              <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 space-y-2">
                <li>• Admission & discharge category mapping (mCIDE)</li>
                <li>• Age calculation & filtering</li>
                <li>• Geographic variable cleaning (FIPS codes)</li>
              </ul>
              <div class="mt-3 p-3 bg-gray-50 rounded text-xs">
                <strong>Composite Key:</strong> hospitalization_id
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="flip-card-back bg-clif-burgundy rounded-lg shadow-md p-6 text-white overflow-y-auto">
              <button class="modal-close" aria-label="Close">×</button>
              <h4 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Hospitalization</h4>

              <div class="expanded-content">
                <div class="space-y-6">
                  <!-- Important Notes -->
                  <div class="bg-yellow-500/20 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-400/30">
                    <h5 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2 text-yellow-300">Important Notes</h5>
                    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
                      <li>• If a patient is discharged to Home/Hospice (e.g., a <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">discharge_name</code> like "Hospice - Home"), then <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">discharge_category == hospice</code></li>
                      <li>• Mortality is identified by <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">discharge_category == expired</code>; some studies also count <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">hospice</code> as a death outcome</li>
                      <li>• Geographic indicators (<code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">zipcode_nine_digit</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">census_block_code</code>, etc.) should be added if available. <strong>zipcode_nine_digit</strong> is preferred over zipcode_five_digit; <strong>census_block_code</strong> is ideal for census-based indicators</li>
                      <li>• If a patient is <strong>transferred between different hospitals</strong> within a health system, create a <strong>new hospitalization_id</strong></li>
                      <li>• If a patient is seen in ER at hospital A then admitted to inpatient at hospital B, use <strong>one hospitalization_id</strong> for both stays</li>
                      <li>• A <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">hospitalization_joined_id</code> can be created from contiguous hospitalization_ids</li>
                    </ul>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 1 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 1: Create Hospitalization Mappings</h5>
                    <p class="text-sm mb-3">Before transforming your hospitalization data, prepare the mapping files:</p>
                    <div class="space-y-3 text-sm">
                      <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg">
                        <p><strong class="text-blue-300">a. Admission Type Mapping:</strong> Map <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">admission_type_name</code> to <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">admission_type_category</code>. Permissible values: <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">ed</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">facility</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">osh</code> (outside hospital), <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">direct</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">elective</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">other</code></p>
                        <a href="https://github.com/Common-Longitudinal-ICU-data-Format/CLIF/blob/3.0/mCIDE/hospitalization/clif_hospitalization_admission_type_categories.csv" target="_blank" class="text-blue-300 hover:underline text-xs mt-1 inline-block">→ clif_hospitalization_admission_type_categories.csv</a>
                      </div>
                      <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg">
                        <p><strong class="text-blue-300">b. Discharge Mapping:</strong> Map <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">discharge_name</code> to <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">discharge_category</code>. Permissible values (lowercase snake_case): <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">home</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">snf</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">expired</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">acute_ip_rehab</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">hospice</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">ltach</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">acute_care_hosp</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">group_home</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">chemical_dependency</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">ama</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">assisted_living</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">still_admitted</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">missing</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">other</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">mental_health_hosp</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">shelter</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">jail</code></p>
                        <a href="https://github.com/Common-Longitudinal-ICU-data-Format/CLIF/blob/3.0/mCIDE/hospitalization/clif_hospitalization_discharge_categories.csv" target="_blank" class="text-blue-300 hover:underline text-xs mt-1 inline-block">→ clif_hospitalization_discharge_categories.csv</a>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 2 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 2: Filter to Inpatient Hospitalizations</h5>
                    <p class="text-sm">Filter your hospitalization data to include only inpatient hospitalizations.</p>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 3 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 3: Apply Mappings</h5>
                    <p class="text-sm">Join the mapping files created in Step 1 to add <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">admission_type_category</code> and <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">discharge_category</code> columns.</p>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 4 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 4: Age Calculation & Filtering</h5>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-sm">
                      <ul class="space-y-2">
                        <li>• If <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">age_at_admission</code> is not present, calculate it using <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">birth_date</code></li>
                        <li>• <strong class="text-red-300">Drop encounters</strong> where age &gt; 120 years or &lt; 18 years</li>
                      </ul>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="space-y-6">
                  <!-- Step 5 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 5: Clean Geographic Variables</h5>
                    <p class="text-sm mb-3">Clean and standardize FIPS codes by removing spaces, dashes, and special characters:</p>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-2 rounded-lg overflow-x-auto mb-3">
                      <table class="text-xs w-full">
                        <thead>
                          <tr class="border-b border-white/20">
                            <th class="px-2 py-1 text-left">Variable</th>
                            <th class="px-2 py-1 text-left">Digits</th>
                            <th class="px-2 py-1 text-left">Description</th>
                          </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody class="text-xs">
                          <tr class="border-b border-white/10"><td class="px-2 py-1"><code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">state_code</code></td><td class="px-2 py-1 text-green-300">2</td><td class="px-2 py-1">State FIPS</td></tr>
                          <tr class="border-b border-white/10"><td class="px-2 py-1"><code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">county_code</code></td><td class="px-2 py-1 text-green-300">5</td><td class="px-2 py-1">State + County</td></tr>
                          <tr class="border-b border-white/10"><td class="px-2 py-1"><code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">census_tract</code></td><td class="px-2 py-1 text-green-300">11</td><td class="px-2 py-1">State + County + Tract</td></tr>
                          <tr class="border-b border-white/10"><td class="px-2 py-1"><code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">census_block_group_code</code></td><td class="px-2 py-1 text-green-300">12</td><td class="px-2 py-1">Tract + Block Group</td></tr>
                          <tr><td class="px-2 py-1"><code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">census_block_code</code></td><td class="px-2 py-1 text-green-300">15</td><td class="px-2 py-1">Full Block ID</td></tr>
                        </tbody>
                      </table>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-xs">
                      <p class="text-yellow-300 font-semibold mb-2">Derive from census_block_code:</p>
                      <div class="font-mono space-y-1">
                        <div>state_code = census_block_code[0:2]</div>
                        <div>county_code = census_block_code[0:5]</div>
                        <div>census_tract = census_block_code[0:11]</div>
                        <div>census_block_group_code = census_block_code[0:12]</div>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-xs mt-3">
                      <p class="text-blue-300 font-semibold mb-1">fips_version:</p>
                      <p>Year of Census geography definitions (2000, 2010, 2020)</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 6 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 6: Final Cleanup</h5>
                    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">•</span>
                        <span><strong>Deduplicate:</strong> Remove duplicate rows by composite key <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">hospitalization_id</code></span>
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">•</span>
                        <span><strong>UTC Conversion:</strong> Convert all datetime fields to UTC timezone</span>
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">•</span>
                        <span><strong>Data Types:</strong> Ensure all variables match data dictionary specifications</span>
                      </li>
                    </ul>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Data Quality Checks -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Data Quality Checks</h5>
                    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">✓</span>
                        <span>Ensure <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">discharge_dttm</code> ≥ <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">admission_dttm</code></span>
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">✓</span>
                        <span>Verify FIPS codes have correct digit lengths</span>
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">✓</span>
                        <span>Validate category mappings against mCIDE</span>
                      </li>
                    </ul>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Labs -->
        <div id="labs" class="flip-card h-64 cursor-pointer">
          <div class="flip-card-inner">
            <div class="flip-card-front bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-6 border border-gray-200">
              <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-4 text-gray-800 flex items-center justify-between">
                labs
                <span class="text-xs text-gray-500">Click to flip</span>
              </h4>
              <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 space-y-2">
                <li>• Lab order & category mapping (mCIDE)</li>
                <li>• Specimen mapping: plasma_blood, urine, pleural, peritoneal, bal</li>
                <li>• Unit standardization to CLIF reference units</li>
                <li>• Numeric value parsing</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="flip-card-back bg-clif-burgundy rounded-lg shadow-md p-6 text-white overflow-y-auto">
              <button class="modal-close" aria-label="Close">×</button>
              <h4 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Labs</h4>

              <div class="expanded-content">
                <div class="space-y-6">
                  <!-- Step 1 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 1: Create Lab Mappings</h5>
                    <p class="text-sm mb-3">Before transforming your lab data, prepare the mapping files:</p>
                    <div class="space-y-3 text-sm">
                      <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg">
                        <p><strong class="text-blue-300">a. Lab Order Mapping:</strong> Map <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">lab_order_name</code> to <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">lab_order_category</code></p>
                        <a href="https://github.com/Common-Longitudinal-ICU-data-Format/CLIF/blob/3.0/mCIDE/labs/clif_labs_order_categories.csv" target="_blank" class="text-blue-300 hover:underline text-xs mt-1 inline-block">→ clif_labs_order_categories.csv</a>
                      </div>
                      <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg">
                        <p><strong class="text-blue-300">b. Lab Category Mapping:</strong> Map <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">lab_name</code> to <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">lab_category</code></p>
                        <a href="https://github.com/Common-Longitudinal-ICU-data-Format/CLIF/blob/3.0/mCIDE/labs/clif_lab_categories.csv" target="_blank" class="text-blue-300 hover:underline text-xs mt-1 inline-block">→ clif_lab_categories.csv</a>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 2 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 2: Filter to Inpatient Hospitalizations</h5>
                    <p class="text-sm">Filter your lab data to include only inpatient hospitalizations.</p>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 3 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 3: Apply Mappings</h5>
                    <p class="text-sm">Join the mapping files created in Step 1 to add <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">lab_order_category</code> and <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">lab_category</code> columns.</p>
                    <div class="bg-blue-500/20 p-3 rounded-lg border border-blue-400/30 text-sm mt-3">
                      <p class="text-blue-300 font-semibold mb-2">Multi-value cells:</p>
                      <p class="mb-2">In <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">clif_lab_categories.csv</code>, an analyte valid for more than one panel or specimen lists them slash-delimited — <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">potassium</code> shows <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">bmp/poc</code>. That list is what the analyte <em>permits</em>, not what a given result <em>is</em>.</p>
                      <p><strong>Emit one CLIF row per lab result</strong> and resolve each cell to the single applicable value. Never create a row per slash-separated value.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-sm mt-3">
                      <p class="mb-2">Point-of-care example — POC results can differ in accuracy from the central lab, so the panel keeps them separable without a separate <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">lab_category</code>:</p>
                      <ul class="space-y-1 text-xs">
                        <li>• Potassium off a BMP → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">lab_category = potassium</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">lab_order_category = bmp</code></li>
                        <li>• POC potassium (bedside or gas analyzer) → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">lab_category = potassium</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">lab_order_category = poc</code></li>
                      </ul>
                      <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-gray-300">Also applies to bicarbonate, creatinine, glucose, hematocrit, lactate, and sodium. Fingerstick glucometer glucose has its own panel: <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">glucose</code> + <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">fingerstick</code>, not <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">poc</code>.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-blue-500/20 p-3 rounded-lg border border-blue-400/30 text-sm mt-3">
                      <p class="text-blue-300 font-semibold mb-2">Blood gas results — <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">blood_gas</code> or <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">poc</code>?</p>
                      <p class="mb-2"><strong>Step 1: where was it run?</strong> If the result came from a point-of-care device (a bedside analyzer; the order or result name usually says POC, iSTAT, or bedside), <strong>every analyte on it is <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">poc</code></strong> — pH, pO2, pCO2, sO2 and HCO3⁻ included. <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">lab_category</code> is unchanged (<code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">ph_arterial</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">po2_arterial</code>, …); only the panel differs.</p>
                      <p class="mb-2"><strong>Step 2: central-lab gas analyzer.</strong> Otherwise, once you have mapped the result to its <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">lab_category</code>, look it up here:</p>
                      <table class="w-full text-xs border-collapse mb-2">
                        <thead>
                          <tr class="border-b border-white/30">
                            <th class="text-left py-1 pr-2 font-semibold">If <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">lab_category</code> is…</th>
                            <th class="text-left py-1 font-semibold">then <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">lab_order_category</code> is</th>
                          </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                          <tr class="border-b border-white/10">
                            <td class="py-1 pr-2"><code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">ph_*</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">pco2_*</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">po2_*</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">so2_*</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">bicarbonate</code> (when reported alongside the gas values)</td>
                            <td class="py-1"><code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">blood_gas</code></td>
                          </tr>
                          <tr class="border-b border-white/10">
                            <td class="py-1 pr-2"><code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">sodium</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">potassium</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">glucose</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">lactate</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">hematocrit</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">creatinine</code></td>
                            <td class="py-1"><code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">poc</code></td>
                          </tr>
                          <tr class="border-b border-white/10">
                            <td class="py-1 pr-2">any other analyte (e.g. <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">chloride</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">calcium_ionized</code>)</td>
                            <td class="py-1">that analyte's own permitted panel in <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">clif_lab_categories.csv</code> — <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">chloride</code> → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">bmp</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">calcium_ionized</code> → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">misc</code></td>
                          </tr>
                          <tr>
                            <td class="py-1 pr-2">the co-oximetry "hemoglobin/saturation" hemoglobin reported with the gas</td>
                            <td class="py-1">do not map — it is not <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">hemoglobin</code> (that category is CBC hemoglobin only)</td>
                          </tr>
                        </tbody>
                      </table>
                      <p class="text-xs text-gray-300">One central-lab gas order can therefore produce rows in several panels. Mixed-venous gases from the central lab use <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">mixed_venous_blood_gas</code> instead of <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">blood_gas</code>. Finger-stick glucometer glucose is <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">fingerstick</code>, not <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">poc</code>. <em>Why:</em> POC results can differ in accuracy from the central lab, so anything from a bedside device is kept separable as <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">poc</code>; and even on a central-lab gas analyzer the sodium, potassium, etc. are measured by an electrode method rather than the chemistry assay, so those stay <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">poc</code> too. (Decision confirmed by the labs working group, Oct 2026.)</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-sm mt-3">
                      <p class="mb-2">Bicarbonate vs. CO2:</p>
                      <ul class="space-y-1 text-xs">
                        <li>• BMP bicarbonate (often reported as "CO2") → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">bicarbonate</code> + <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">bmp</code></li>
                        <li>• HCO3⁻ from a point-of-care device (bedside analyzer) → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">bicarbonate</code> + <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">poc</code></li>
                        <li>• HCO3⁻ reported alongside gas values on a central-lab gas analyzer → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">bicarbonate</code> + <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">blood_gas</code></li>
                        <li>• pCO2 → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">pco2_arterial</code> / <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">pco2_venous</code>, never bicarbonate</li>
                        <li>• Total CO2 (tCO2, reported by some gas analyzers) → do not map</li>
                        <li>• Co-oximetry "hemoglobin/saturation" off a gas → do not map (not <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">hemoglobin</code>; it disagrees with CBC hemoglobin)</li>
                      </ul>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 4 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 4: Map Specimen Types</h5>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-sm">
                      <p class="text-green-300 font-semibold mb-2">Keep rows whose specimen maps to one of the five <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">lab_specimen_category</code> values:</p>
                      <ul class="space-y-1 text-xs mb-2">
                        <li>• <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">plasma_blood</code> — whole blood, plasma, or serum (default for systemic labs)</li>
                        <li>• <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">urine</code></li>
                        <li>• <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">pleural</code> — pleural fluid from thoracentesis or pleural catheter</li>
                        <li>• <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">peritoneal</code> — peritoneal / ascitic fluid from paracentesis or peritoneal catheter</li>
                        <li>• <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">bal</code> — bronchoalveolar lavage fluid</li>
                      </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-blue-500/20 p-3 rounded-lg border border-blue-400/30 text-sm mt-3">
                      <p class="text-blue-300 font-semibold mb-2">Blood specimens:</p>
                      <p>For mapping purposes, we use <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">plasma_blood</code> as a broad category encompassing whole blood, plasma, and serum, while recognizing that individual labs may be performed using different blood components. Sites do not need to distinguish serum from plasma from whole blood — all three map to <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">plasma_blood</code>.</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 5 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 5: Merge Sensitive Lab Variants</h5>
                    <div class="bg-blue-500/20 p-3 rounded-lg border border-blue-400/30 text-sm mb-3">
                      <p class="text-blue-300 font-semibold mb-2">Important:</p>
                      <p>Map both regular and highly sensitive lab assays to the same <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">lab_category</code>.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-sm">
                      <p class="mb-2">Examples:</p>
                      <ul class="space-y-1 text-xs">
                        <li>• Troponin I (ng/mL) + hs-Troponin I (ng/L) → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">troponin_i</code></li>
                        <li>• CRP (mg/L) + hs-CRP (mg/L) → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">crp</code></li>
                      </ul>
                      <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-gray-300">Note: Unit conversions will be handled in the next step.</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="space-y-6">
                  <!-- Step 6 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 6: Standardize Reference Units</h5>
                    <div class="bg-yellow-500/20 p-3 rounded-lg border border-yellow-400/30 text-sm mb-3">
                      <p class="text-yellow-300 font-semibold mb-2">Critical Requirement:</p>
                      <p>All lab values must be reported using CLIF reference units. Only listed reference units are permissible for respective lab categories. Sites must convert raw values during ETL.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-sm">
                      <p>Reference units for each lab category:</p>
                      <a href="https://github.com/Common-Longitudinal-ICU-data-Format/CLIF/blob/3.0/mCIDE/labs/clif_lab_categories.csv" target="_blank" class="text-blue-300 hover:underline text-xs mt-1 inline-block">→ clif_lab_categories.csv (reference_unit column)</a>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 7 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 7: Create Numeric Value Field</h5>
                    <p class="text-sm mb-2">Create <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">lab_value_numeric</code> by parsing the character field <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">lab_value</code> to extract only the numeric part of the string.</p>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-2 rounded-lg text-xs font-mono">
                      lab_value_numeric = parse_number(lab_value)
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 8 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 8: Final Cleanup</h5>
                    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">•</span>
                        <strong>Deduplicate:</strong> Remove duplicate rows
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">•</span>
                        <strong>UTC Conversion:</strong> Convert all datetime fields to UTC timezone
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">•</span>
                        <strong>Data Types:</strong> Ensure all variables match data dictionary specifications
                      </li>
                    </ul>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Data Quality Checks -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Data Quality Checks</h5>
                    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">✓</span>
                        Validate <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">lab_category</code> mappings against mCIDE
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">✓</span>
                        Verify all units match CLIF reference units
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">✓</span>
                        Check <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">lab_value_numeric</code> parsing accuracy
                      </li>
                    </ul>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Medication Admin Continuous -->
        <div id="medication-admin-continuous" class="flip-card h-64 cursor-pointer">
          <div class="flip-card-inner">
            <div class="flip-card-front bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-6 border border-gray-200">
              <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-4 text-gray-800 flex items-center justify-between">
                medication_admin_continuous
                <span class="text-xs text-gray-500">Click to flip</span>
              </h4>
              <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 space-y-2">
                <li>• MAR action & med category mapping (mCIDE)</li>
                <li>• Filter continuous medications</li>
                <li>• Combination drug handling</li>
                <li>• Trial drugs & placebos</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="flip-card-back bg-clif-burgundy rounded-lg shadow-md p-6 text-white overflow-y-auto">
              <button class="modal-close" aria-label="Close">×</button>
              <h4 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Medication Admin Continuous</h4>

              <div class="expanded-content">
                <div class="space-y-6">
                  <!-- Step 1 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 1: Create Medication Mappings</h5>
                    <p class="text-sm mb-3">Before transforming your medication data, prepare the mapping files:</p>
                    <div class="space-y-3 text-sm">
                      <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg">
                        <p><strong class="text-blue-300">a. Action Category Mapping:</strong> Map <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">mar_action_name</code> → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">mar_action_category</code>. The same CSV gives each category's <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">mar_action_group</code> (<code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">administered</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">not_administered</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">other</code>) — carry it into the table.</p>
                        <a href="https://github.com/Common-Longitudinal-ICU-data-Format/CLIF/blob/3.0/mCIDE/medication_admin_continuous/clif_medication_admin_continuous_action_categories.csv" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-blue-300 hover:underline text-xs mt-1 inline-block">→ clif_medication_admin_continuous_action_categories.csv</a>
                      </div>
                      <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg">
                        <p><strong class="text-blue-300">b. Med Category Mapping:</strong> Map <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_name</code> → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_category</code></p>
                        <a href="https://github.com/Common-Longitudinal-ICU-data-Format/CLIF/blob/3.0/mCIDE/medication_admin_continuous/clif_medication_admin_continuous_med_categories.csv" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-blue-300 hover:underline text-xs mt-1 inline-block">→ clif_medication_admin_continuous_med_categories.csv</a>
                      </div>
                      <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg">
                        <p><strong class="text-blue-300">c. Route Category Mapping:</strong> Map <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_route_name</code> → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_route_category</code></p>
                        <a href="https://github.com/Common-Longitudinal-ICU-data-Format/CLIF/blob/3.0/mCIDE/medication_admin_continuous/clif_medication_admin_continuous_med_route_categories.csv" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-blue-300 hover:underline text-xs mt-1 inline-block">→ clif_medication_admin_continuous_med_route_categories.csv</a>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 2 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 2: Filter to Inpatient Hospitalizations</h5>
                    <p class="text-sm">Filter your medication data to include only inpatient hospitalizations.</p>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 3 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 3: Apply Mappings</h5>
                    <p class="text-sm">Join the mapping files to add category columns.</p>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-sm mt-3">
                      <p class="text-yellow-300 font-semibold mb-2">Recording the end of an infusion:</p>
                      <p class="text-xs">There is no end-time column; each row records a rate change. When an infusion stops or pauses, write a new row with <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_dose = 0</code>, the raw <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">mar_action_name</code> (e.g. "Stopped", "Paused"), <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">mar_action_category = stop</code> and <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">mar_action_group = not_administered</code>.</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 4 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 4: Filter Continuous Medications & Standardize Units</h5>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-sm">
                      <p class="mb-2">Keep the rows whose <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_name</code> maps to a <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_category</code> in <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">clif_medication_admin_continuous_med_categories.csv</code>. Do not filter on the unit string: a regex such as <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">min|hr|day</code> drops five categories whose standard unit has no time component — <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">albuterol</code> (mg), <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">terbutaline</code> (mg), <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">baclofen</code> (ml), <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">ipratropium</code> (ml), <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">nitric_oxide</code> (ppm).</p>
                      <p class="text-xs">Some categories (e.g. <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">fentanyl</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">propofol</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">heparin</code>) appear in both the continuous and the intermittent CSV. A dose charted as a quantity per unit time (a running infusion) belongs here; a fixed quantity given at one time (a bolus) belongs in <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">medication_admin_intermittent</code>.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-xs mt-2">
                      <p class="text-blue-300 font-semibold mb-2">Convert to the category's unit:</p>
                      <p>Each <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_category</code> has one <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_dose_unit</code> in the CSV (e.g. <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">fentanyl</code> → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">mcg/hr</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">propofol</code> → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">mcg/kg/min</code>). Convert the raw rate into it; if the raw rate is in mL/hr, use the concentration in <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_name</code>. Weight-based units (per kg) need the patient's weight.</p>
                      <p class="mt-1 text-gray-300">e.g. "FENTANYL 2500 MCG/50 ML IV INFUSION" running at 2 mL/hr → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_dose = 100</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_dose_unit = mcg/hr</code></p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-xs mt-2">
                      <p class="text-blue-300 font-semibold mb-2">Also record the pump rate:</p>
                      <p><code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">volume_infusion_rate</code> is the fluid volume per time (e.g. 2 mL/hr), separate from <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_dose</code>, which is the drug quantity per time. Fill <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">volume_infusion_rate_unit</code> from the CSV's <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">volume_infusion_rate_units</code> column (<code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">ml/hr</code> for pumped infusions; <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">NA</code> for inhaled categories such as <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">albuterol</code> and <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">nitric_oxide</code>).</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 5 - Inhaled Nitric Oxide -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 5: Special Case - Inhaled Nitric Oxide</h5>
                    <div class="bg-yellow-500/20 p-3 rounded-lg border border-yellow-400/30 text-sm">
                      <p>If inhaled nitric oxide is not in your medication admin table, refer to <strong>flowsheets data</strong>. The order typically goes in as an RT order (not medication order) and is documented in flowsheets rather than MAR. Map it to <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">nitric_oxide</code> with <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_dose_unit = ppm</code>; it is a continuous-only category.</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="space-y-6">
                  <!-- Step 6 - Combination Drugs -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 6: Handle Combination & Trial Drugs</h5>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">A. Combination Drugs</h5>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-sm mb-3">
                      <p class="text-yellow-300 font-semibold mb-2">One row per administration:</p>
                      <p class="text-xs mb-2">Do not split a combination product into one row per component. First check whether the CSV lists the combination itself as a <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_category</code>; if so, use it. Otherwise map the row to the <strong>primary active ingredient</strong> — the dictionary's example is <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">ACETAMIN-CALCIUM-MAG-CAFFEINE ORAL</code> → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">acetaminophen</code>. The 3.0 continuous CSV has no combination categories, so continuous combinations always map to the primary ingredient.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-xs">
                      <p class="text-green-300 font-semibold mb-2">Example: "MedA-MedB 7.5-325 MG/15 ML" running at 30 mL/hr</p>
                      <p class="mb-2">If medA_medB is not a CLIF med_category and MedA is the primary ingredient:</p>
                      <div class="space-y-1 ml-2">
                        <p>→ one row: med_category = "medA", med_dose = 15, med_dose_unit = medA's unit in the CSV (here mg/hr)</p>
                      </div>
                      <p class="mt-2 text-gray-300"><code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_name</code> keeps the full raw string, so the other component is not lost.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-xs mt-2">
                      <p class="text-blue-300 font-semibold mb-2">Unit Conversion (mL → the category's med_dose_unit):</p>
                      <p>If the raw rate is in mL/hr, convert to the mapped category's <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_dose_unit</code> using the concentration of the <em>mapped</em> ingredient in <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_name</code> (see Step 4).</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Trial Drugs & Placebos -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">B. Trial Drugs & Placebos</h5>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-sm mb-3">
                      <p class="mb-2">There is no <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">trial_drug</code> category. Map a trial drug to its active ingredient's <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_category</code> like any other row; <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_group</code> then follows from the CSV.</p>
                      <div class="bg-white/10 p-2 rounded text-xs mt-2">
                        <p class="text-yellow-300 font-semibold mb-1">Examples:</p>
                        <p class="text-gray-300">"ACETAMINOPHEN (IRB 140122) 325 MG ORAL TAB"</p>
                        <p class="mt-1">→ med_category: <span class="text-green-300">acetaminophen</span></p>
                        <p class="mt-2 text-gray-300">"ACYCLOVIR OR PLACEBO CAPSULE (IRB 171591) 400 MG"</p>
                        <p class="mt-1">→ the patient may have received placebo, so the active ingredient cannot be known: leave <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_category</code> unmapped (the raw string stays in <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_name</code>)</p>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-blue-300 mr-2">•</span>
                        <span><strong>Brand Names:</strong> Map to the generic active ingredient's <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_category</code>; the raw brand string is preserved in <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_name</code></span>
                      </li>
                    </ul>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 7 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 7: Final Cleanup</h5>
                    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">•</span>
                        <strong>Deduplicate:</strong> Remove duplicate rows
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">•</span>
                        <strong>UTC Conversion:</strong> Convert all datetime fields to UTC timezone
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">•</span>
                        <strong>Data Types:</strong> Ensure all variables match data dictionary specifications
                      </li>
                    </ul>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Data Quality Checks -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Data Quality Checks</h5>
                    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">✓</span>
                        Validate <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_category</code> mappings against mCIDE
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">✓</span>
                        Verify every row's <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_dose_unit</code> equals its category's unit in the CSV
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">✓</span>
                        Check combination and trial drugs produce one row each, mapped to the explicit combo category or the primary active ingredient
                      </li>
                    </ul>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Medication Admin Intermittent -->
        <div id="medication-admin-intermittent" class="flip-card h-64 cursor-pointer">
          <div class="flip-card-inner">
            <div class="flip-card-front bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-6 border border-gray-200">
              <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-4 text-gray-800 flex items-center justify-between">
                medication_admin_intermittent
                <span class="text-xs text-gray-500">Click to flip</span>
              </h4>
              <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 space-y-2">
                <li>• MAR action & med category mapping (mCIDE)</li>
                <li>• Filter intermittent medications</li>
                <li>• Combination drug handling</li>
                <li>• Trial drugs & placebos</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="flip-card-back bg-clif-burgundy rounded-lg shadow-md p-6 text-white overflow-y-auto">
              <button class="modal-close" aria-label="Close">×</button>
              <h4 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Medication Admin Intermittent</h4>

              <div class="expanded-content">
                <div class="space-y-6">
                  <!-- Step 1 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 1: Create Medication Mappings</h5>
                    <p class="text-sm mb-3">Before transforming your medication data, prepare the mapping files:</p>
                    <div class="space-y-3 text-sm">
                      <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg">
                        <p><strong class="text-blue-300">a. Action Category Mapping:</strong> Map <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">mar_action_name</code> → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">mar_action_category</code>. The same CSV gives each category's <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">mar_action_group</code> (<code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">administered</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">not_administered</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">other</code>) — carry it into the table.</p>
                        <a href="https://github.com/Common-Longitudinal-ICU-data-Format/CLIF/blob/3.0/mCIDE/medication_admin_intermittent/clif_medication_admin_intermittent_action_categories.csv" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-blue-300 hover:underline text-xs mt-1 inline-block">→ clif_medication_admin_intermittent_action_categories.csv</a>
                      </div>
                      <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg">
                        <p><strong class="text-blue-300">b. Med Category Mapping:</strong> Map <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_name</code> → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_category</code></p>
                        <a href="https://github.com/Common-Longitudinal-ICU-data-Format/CLIF/blob/3.0/mCIDE/medication_admin_intermittent/clif_medication_admin_intermittent_med_categories.csv" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-blue-300 hover:underline text-xs mt-1 inline-block">→ clif_medication_admin_intermittent_med_categories.csv</a>
                      </div>
                      <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg">
                        <p><strong class="text-blue-300">c. Route Category Mapping:</strong> Map <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_route_name</code> → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_route_category</code></p>
                        <a href="https://github.com/Common-Longitudinal-ICU-data-Format/CLIF/blob/3.0/mCIDE/medication_admin_intermittent/clif_medication_admin_intermittent_med_route_categories.csv" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-blue-300 hover:underline text-xs mt-1 inline-block">→ clif_medication_admin_intermittent_med_route_categories.csv</a>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 2 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 2: Filter to Inpatient Hospitalizations</h5>
                    <p class="text-sm">Filter your medication data to include only inpatient hospitalizations.</p>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 3 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 3: Apply Mappings</h5>
                    <p class="text-sm">Join the mapping files to add category columns.</p>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 4 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 4: Filter Intermittent Medications</h5>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-sm">
                      <p class="mb-2">Keep the rows whose <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_name</code> maps to a <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_category</code> in <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">clif_medication_admin_intermittent_med_categories.csv</code>. Do not filter on the unit string alone.</p>
                      <p class="text-xs">Some categories (e.g. <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">fentanyl</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">propofol</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">heparin</code>) appear in both the intermittent and the continuous CSV. A fixed quantity given at one time (a bolus) belongs here, even for a drug usually run as a drip; a dose charted as a quantity per unit time (a running infusion) belongs in <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">medication_admin_continuous</code>.</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 5 - Standardize med_dose_unit -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 5: Convert to the Category's med_dose_unit</h5>
                    <div class="bg-yellow-500/20 p-3 rounded-lg border border-yellow-400/30 text-sm mb-3">
                      <p class="text-yellow-300 font-semibold mb-2">3.0 requirement:</p>
                      <p>Every intermittent <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_category</code> is tied to one <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_dose_unit</code> in the CSV, drawn from a closed set: <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">mg</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">g</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">mcg</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">mmol</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">ml</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">meq</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">units</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">cells</code>. Convert each raw dose into its category's unit; a single category may not mix units.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-xs">
                      <p class="mb-1">e.g. "AMPICILLIN 2000 MG IV" → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">ampicillin</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_dose = 2</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_dose_unit = g</code></p>
                      <p>If the raw dose is in mL, convert using the concentration in <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_name</code>: "ACETAMINOPHEN 160 MG/5 ML" given as 10 mL → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">acetaminophen</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_dose = 320</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_dose_unit = mg</code>.</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="space-y-6">
                  <!-- Step 6 - Combination Drugs -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 6: Handle Combination & Trial Drugs</h5>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">A. Combination Drugs</h5>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-sm mb-3">
                      <p class="text-yellow-300 font-semibold mb-2">One row per administration:</p>
                      <p class="text-xs mb-2">Do not split a combination product into one row per component. First check whether the CSV lists the combination itself as a <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_category</code> — the 3.0 intermittent CSV has explicit entries such as <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">amoxicillin_clavulanate</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">ampicillin_sulbactam</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">piperacillin_tazobactam</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">trimethoprim_sulfamethoxazole</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">dipyridamole_aspirin</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">sulbactam_durlobactam</code>, <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">sulfadiazine_trimethoprim</code> and others, so search the CSV first. If it does, use it. Otherwise map the row to the <strong>primary active ingredient</strong> — the dictionary's example is <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">ACETAMIN-CALCIUM-MAG-CAFFEINE ORAL</code> → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">acetaminophen</code>.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-xs">
                      <p class="text-green-300 font-semibold mb-2">Example: "MedA-MedB 7.5-325 MG/15 ML" given as 30 mL</p>
                      <p class="mb-2">If medA_medB is not a CLIF med_category and MedA is the primary ingredient:</p>
                      <div class="space-y-1 ml-2">
                        <p>→ one row: med_category = "medA", med_dose = 15, med_dose_unit = medA's unit in the CSV (here mg)</p>
                      </div>
                      <p class="mt-2 text-gray-300"><code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_name</code> keeps the full raw string, so the other component is not lost.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-xs mt-2">
                      <p class="text-blue-300 font-semibold mb-2">Unit Conversion (mL → the category's med_dose_unit):</p>
                      <p>If the raw dose is in mL, convert to the mapped category's <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_dose_unit</code> using the concentration of the <em>mapped</em> ingredient in <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_name</code> (see Step 5).</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Trial Drugs & Placebos -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">B. Trial Drugs & Placebos</h5>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-sm mb-3">
                      <p class="mb-2">There is no <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">trial_drug</code> category. Map a trial drug to its active ingredient's <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_category</code> like any other row; <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_group</code> then follows from the CSV.</p>
                      <div class="bg-white/10 p-2 rounded text-xs mt-2">
                        <p class="text-yellow-300 font-semibold mb-1">Examples:</p>
                        <p class="text-gray-300">"ACETAMINOPHEN (IRB 140122) 325 MG ORAL TAB"</p>
                        <p class="mt-1">→ med_category: <span class="text-green-300">acetaminophen</span></p>
                        <p class="mt-2 text-gray-300">"ACYCLOVIR OR PLACEBO CAPSULE (IRB 171591) 400 MG"</p>
                        <p class="mt-1">→ the patient may have received placebo, so the active ingredient cannot be known: leave <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_category</code> unmapped (the raw string stays in <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_name</code>)</p>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-blue-300 mr-2">•</span>
                        <span><strong>Brand Names:</strong> Map to the generic active ingredient's <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_category</code>; the raw brand string is preserved in <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_name</code></span>
                      </li>
                    </ul>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 7 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 7: Final Cleanup</h5>
                    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">•</span>
                        <strong>Deduplicate:</strong> Remove duplicate rows
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">•</span>
                        <strong>UTC Conversion:</strong> Convert all datetime fields to UTC timezone
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">•</span>
                        <strong>Data Types:</strong> Ensure all variables match data dictionary specifications
                      </li>
                    </ul>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Data Quality Checks -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Data Quality Checks</h5>
                    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">✓</span>
                        Validate <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_category</code> mappings against mCIDE
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">✓</span>
                        Verify every row's <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">med_dose_unit</code> equals its category's unit in the CSV
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">✓</span>
                        Check combination and trial drugs produce one row each, mapped to the explicit combo category or the primary active ingredient
                      </li>
                    </ul>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Patient -->
        <div id="patient" class="flip-card h-64 cursor-pointer">
          <div class="flip-card-inner">
            <div class="flip-card-front bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-6 border border-gray-200">
              <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-4 text-gray-800 flex items-center justify-between">
                patient
                <span class="text-xs text-gray-500">Click to flip</span>
              </h4>
              <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 space-y-2">
                <li>• Demographics mapping (mCIDE)</li>
                <li>• Handle missing category values</li>
                <li>• One record per patient_id</li>
              </ul>
              <div class="mt-3 p-3 bg-gray-50 rounded text-xs">
                <strong>Composite Key:</strong> patient_id
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="flip-card-back bg-clif-burgundy rounded-lg shadow-md p-6 text-white overflow-y-auto">
              <button class="modal-close" aria-label="Close">×</button>
              <h4 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Patient</h4>

              <div class="expanded-content">
                <div class="space-y-6">
                  <!-- Step 1 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 1: Create Patient Mappings</h5>
                    <p class="text-sm mb-3">Before transforming your patient data, prepare the mapping files:</p>
                    <div class="space-y-3 text-sm">
                      <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg">
                        <p><strong class="text-blue-300">a. Race Category Mapping:</strong> Map <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">race_name</code> → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">race_category</code></p>
                        <a href="https://github.com/Common-Longitudinal-ICU-data-Format/CLIF/blob/3.0/mCIDE/patient/clif_patient_race_categories.csv" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-blue-300 hover:underline text-xs mt-1 inline-block">→ clif_patient_race_categories.csv</a>
                      </div>
                      <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg">
                        <p><strong class="text-blue-300">b. Sex Category Mapping:</strong> Map <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">sex_name</code> → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">sex_category</code></p>
                        <a href="https://github.com/Common-Longitudinal-ICU-data-Format/CLIF/blob/3.0/mCIDE/patient/clif_patient_sex_categories.csv" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-blue-300 hover:underline text-xs mt-1 inline-block">→ clif_patient_sex_categories.csv</a>
                      </div>
                      <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg">
                        <p><strong class="text-blue-300">c. Ethnicity Category Mapping:</strong> Map <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">ethnicity_name</code> → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">ethnicity_category</code></p>
                        <a href="https://github.com/Common-Longitudinal-ICU-data-Format/CLIF/blob/3.0/mCIDE/patient/clif_patient_ethinicity_categories.csv" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-blue-300 hover:underline text-xs mt-1 inline-block">→ clif_patient_ethinicity_categories.csv</a>
                      </div>
                      <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg">
                        <p><strong class="text-blue-300">d. Language Category Mapping:</strong> Map <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">language_name</code> → <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">language_category</code></p>
                        <a href="https://github.com/Common-Longitudinal-ICU-data-Format/CLIF/blob/3.0/mCIDE/patient/clif_patient_language_categories.csv" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-blue-300 hover:underline text-xs mt-1 inline-block">→ clif_patient_language_categories.csv</a>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 2 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 2: Filter to Inpatient Patients</h5>
                    <p class="text-sm">Filter your patient data to include only patients whose <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">patient_id</code> appears in your CLIF hospitalization table. The patient table has no <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">hospitalization_id</code>.</p>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 3 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 3: Apply Mappings & Handle Missing Values</h5>
                    <p class="text-sm mb-3">Join the mapping files to add category columns, then fill missing values:</p>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-sm">
                      <p class="text-yellow-300 font-semibold mb-2">Fill missing/null values (every patient CSV has a lowercase <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">unknown</code> category):</p>
                      <ul class="space-y-1 text-xs">
                        <li>• <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">race_category</code> → <span class="text-green-300">"unknown"</span></li>
                        <li>• <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">sex_category</code> → <span class="text-green-300">"unknown"</span></li>
                        <li>• <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">ethnicity_category</code> → <span class="text-green-300">"unknown"</span></li>
                        <li>• <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">language_category</code> → <span class="text-green-300">"unknown"</span></li>
                      </ul>
                      <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-gray-300">Optional: <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">language_interpreter</code> = 1 if the EHR flags the patient as needing a medical interpreter, else 0.</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="space-y-6">
                  <!-- Step 4 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 4: Handle External Death Data Sources</h5>
                    <p class="text-sm mb-3">If using an external source like a state vital records registry to extract <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">death_dttm</code> and the death records are only in date format (no timestamp):</p>
                    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">1.</span>
                        <span><strong>Same day as discharge:</strong> If the external death date matches the patient's <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">discharge_dttm</code> date, use the <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">discharge_dttm</code> as the <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">death_dttm</code></span>
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">2.</span>
                        <span><strong>After discharge:</strong> If the death date occurs after <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">discharge_dttm</code>, use the death date and add midnight as the timestamp (format: <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">YYYY-MM-DD 00:00:00+00:00</code>)</span>
                      </li>
                    </ul>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 5 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 5: Final Cleanup</h5>
                    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">•</span>
                        <span><strong>Deduplicate:</strong> Remove duplicate rows by composite key <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">patient_id</code>. Ensure one record per patient_id</span>
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">•</span>
                        <span><strong>UTC Conversion:</strong> Convert all datetime fields to UTC timezone</span>
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">•</span>
                        <span><strong>Data Types:</strong> Ensure all variables match data dictionary specifications</span>
                      </li>
                    </ul>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Data Quality Checks -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Data Quality Checks</h5>
                    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">✓</span>
                        <span>Ensure one record per <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">patient_id</code></span>
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">✓</span>
                        <span>Validate all category mappings against mCIDE</span>
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">✓</span>
                        <span>Verify no null values remain in category fields</span>
                      </li>
                    </ul>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Patient Assessments -->
        <div id="patient-assessments" class="flip-card h-64 cursor-pointer">
          <div class="flip-card-inner">
            <div class="flip-card-front bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-6 border border-gray-200">
              <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-4 text-gray-800 flex items-center justify-between">
                patient_assessments
