                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 2: Filter to Inpatient Hospitalizations</h5>
                    <p class="text-sm">Filter to inpatient hospitalizations. Keep all codes for those hospitalizations.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="space-y-6">
                  <!-- Step 3 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 3: Populate the 3.0 Columns</h5>
                    <p class="text-sm mb-3">The 3.0 table has six columns:</p>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-xs space-y-1">
                      <div>• <span class="font-mono text-yellow-300">hospitalization_id</span></div>
                      <div>• <span class="font-mono text-yellow-300">billing_provider_id</span> — ID of the provider who billed the procedure</div>
                      <div>• <span class="font-mono text-yellow-300">performing_provider_id</span> — ID of the provider who performed it</div>
                      <div>• <span class="font-mono text-yellow-300">procedure_code</span> — the code itself (valid CPT, ICD-10-PCS or HCPCS code)</div>
                      <div>• <span class="font-mono text-yellow-300">procedure_code_format</span> — one of <span class="font-mono">CPT</span>, <span class="font-mono">ICD10PCS</span>, <span class="font-mono">HCPCS</span></div>
                      <div>• <span class="font-mono text-yellow-300">procedure_billed_dttm</span> — when the procedure was billed (may differ from when it was performed), in UTC</div>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 4 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 4: Final Cleanup</h5>
                    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">•</span>
                        <strong>Deduplicate:</strong> Remove duplicate rows
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">•</span>
                        <strong>UTC Conversion:</strong> Convert all datetime fields to UTC timezone
                      </li>
                      <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">•</span>
                        <strong>Data Types:</strong> Ensure all variables match data dictionary specifications
                      </li>
                    </ul>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Date-Only Columns Tip -->
                  <div class="bg-blue-500/20 p-4 rounded-lg border border-blue-400/30">
                    <h5 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2 text-blue-300">Date-Only Columns</h5>
                    <p class="text-sm mb-2">When your source data only contains a date (no time component):</p>
                    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
                      <li>• Set the time to midnight (00:00:00) in your local timezone</li>
                      <li>• Make it timezone-aware</li>
                      <li>• Then convert to UTC</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p class="text-sm mt-3 text-blue-200">
                      <strong>Example:</strong> A date of 2021-08-26 becomes 2021-08-26 00:00:00 local time,
                      which converts to 2021-08-26 05:00:00+00:00 UTC (for US/Central timezone).
                    </p>
                  </div>

