                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 3 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 3: Apply the Two-Value Rule</h5>
                    <p class="text-sm mb-3"><code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">position_category</code> has exactly two permitted values. The rule is mechanical: anything that documents the patient lying <strong>face-down</strong> (on their stomach) is <span class="font-mono text-green-300">prone</span>; <strong>every other</strong> documented position is <span class="font-mono text-blue-300">not_prone</span>.</p>

                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-sm mb-3">
                      <p class="text-yellow-300 font-semibold mb-2">Keep bed-angle rows:</p>
                      <p class="text-xs mb-2">Do not drop rows that only describe the bed (head-of-bed angle, Trendelenburg, which is the bed tilted head-down). They are documented positions and map to <span class="font-mono text-blue-300">not_prone</span>. The data dictionary example keeps "30 Degrees" as not_prone.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-sm mb-3">
                      <p class="text-yellow-300 font-semibold mb-2">Combined records:</p>
                      <p class="text-xs mb-2">When one field documents several things at once, the row is prone if any part of it documents face-down positioning:</p>
                      <div class="text-xs space-y-1">
                        <div>• "prone/trendelenburg" → <span class="text-green-300">prone</span></div>
                        <div>• "supine, HOB 30 degrees" → <span class="text-blue-300">not_prone</span></div>
                        <div>• "Supine–turn intolerant,microturn L;Supine–back" → <span class="text-blue-300">not_prone</span></div>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 4 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 4: Derive position_category</h5>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg">
                      <div class="text-sm">
                        <p class="mb-2 text-yellow-300 font-semibold">Prone detection using regex, everything else not_prone:</p>
                        <div class="font-mono text-xs bg-white/10 p-2 rounded">
mutate(position_category = if_else(<br/>
&nbsp;&nbsp;str_detect(position_name, regex("prone|face down|swimm", ignore_case = TRUE)),<br/>
&nbsp;&nbsp;"prone", "not_prone"))
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-xs mt-2">Review the distinct <code class="bg-white/20 px-1 rounded">position_name</code> values the regex matches before trusting it. A name that mentions prone but documents something else (e.g., a note that the patient could not tolerate proning) must be mapped by hand.</p>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="space-y-6">
                  <!-- Position Categories -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Position Categories</h5>
                    <p class="text-xs mb-3">Example source names from the mCIDE file and the data dictionary:</p>
                    <div class="space-y-3 text-sm">
                      <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg">
                        <p class="text-green-300 font-semibold mb-2">prone (lying face down):</p>
                        <div class="space-y-1 text-xs">
                          <div>• "Prone" / "Proning" / "Prone positioning"</div>
                          <div>• "Face Down"</div>
                          <div>• "Prone Positioning for ARDS"</div>
                          <div>• "Prone Ventilation"</div>
                          <div>• "Swimming Position"</div>
                        </div>
                      </div>

                      <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg">
                        <p class="text-blue-300 font-semibold mb-2">not_prone (any other position):</p>
                        <div class="space-y-1 text-xs">
                          <div>• "Supine" / "Supine–turn R" / "Supine–back"</div>
                          <div>• "Semi-Fowler's" (head of bed raised partway)</div>
                          <div>• "30 Degrees" and other bed angles</div>
                          <div>• "Trendelenburg" / "Reverse Trendelenburg"</div>
                        </div>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-xs mt-3">
                      <a href="https://github.com/Common-Longitudinal-ICU-data-Format/CLIF/blob/3.0/mCIDE/position/clif_position_categories.csv" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-blue-300 hover:underline">→ clif_position_categories.csv</a>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 5 -->
                  <div>
