                            <td class="py-1">Percent (%)</td>
                          </tr>
                        </tbody>
                      </table>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Step 6 -->
                  <div>
                    <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 6: Optional measured_dttm</h5>
                    <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-xs">
                      <p class="mb-2">3.0 adds an optional <span class="font-mono text-yellow-300">measured_dttm</span> column: when the vital was actually measured at the bedside. It can differ from <span class="font-mono">recorded_dttm</span>, the time the value was entered into the EHR (e.g., vitals written on paper and entered later at shift change).</p>
                      <p>If your source does not distinguish the two timestamps, omit the column or leave it null. Like every datetime, it must be timezone-aware and in UTC.</p>
